<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
  UDP-ONLY FAST DDS PROFILE. The shared-memory transport is disabled here on
  purpose, and this is the evidence that justified it.

  Symptom, five runs across three environment configurations: a separately
  started process could not talk to the stack, while the stack's own nodes
  talked to each other perfectly (fsr_gripper_node read /joint_states without
  trouble). Every readiness probe reported

      joint_state_msgs=0  arm_joints=0  ik=True  followers=0

  Counting could not distinguish the possible causes, so the probe was made to
  print the LISTS instead. That settled it in one run:

      probe sees 1 nodes: ['sim_ready_probe']
      probe sees 81 topics
      /joint_states       publishers=1 subscribers=7  PRESENT in topic list
      /tf                 publishers=1 subscribers=6  PRESENT in topic list
      /robot_description  publishers=1 subscribers=1  PRESENT in topic list

  DISCOVERY IS FINE. The probe found all 81 topics and counted the publishers
  and subscribers correctly -- it knew exactly who was there. What never
  arrived was DATA: zero samples on a topic with one publisher and seven
  subscribers already matched.

  Matched endpoints plus zero delivery is the shared-memory data path failing
  while discovery (UDP multicast) succeeds. Fast DDS said so directly in the
  launch log:

      RTPS_TRANSPORT_SHM Error] Failed init_port fastrtps_port7002:
      open_and_lock_file failed

  CLAUDE.md already records this class -- "stale /dev/shm/fastrtps_* segments
  ... discovery goes intermittent: services appear for one client and not
  another" -- and prescribes clearing them with the stack stopped. That was
  done repeatedly this session (up to 153 segments at a time) and did not fix
  it, so the SHM transport is removed from the data path rather than repaired.

  Everything in this project runs on one machine, so UDP over loopback loses
  nothing but the shared-memory fast path, which is not usable here anyway.

  APPLIES TO BOTH SIDES. It is exported from sim_session.py's SRC, which is
  the single shell prelude used for both the launch and the probe. Setting it
  on only one side would leave them on different transports, which is the very
  failure this file exists to remove.
-->
<dds xmlns="http://www.eprosima.com">
  <profiles>
    <transport_descriptors>
      <transport_descriptor>
        <transport_id>udp_only_transport</transport_id>
        <type>UDPv4</type>
      </transport_descriptor>
    </transport_descriptors>

    <participant profile_name="udp_only_participant" is_default_profile="true">
      <rtps>
        <userTransports>
          <transport_id>udp_only_transport</transport_id>
        </userTransports>
        <!-- Without this the built-in SHM transport is added back alongside
             ours, and the broken path returns. -->
        <useBuiltinTransports>false</useBuiltinTransports>
      </rtps>
    </participant>
  </profiles>
</dds>
